  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nI am the author of IETF Internet-Draft [HTTP Events Query](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-gupta-httpapi-events-query/) (draft-gupta-httpapi-events-query), proposed in the HTTPAPI Working Group. This draft cites the HTML Standard's specification of server-sent events and links to the following anchors:\n\n- `#server-sent-events`: 9.2 Server-sent events\n- `#the-eventsource-interface`: 9.2.2 The `EventSource` interface\n- `#text/event-stream`: 17.7 `text/event-stream`\n\nSection numbers are as of commit 404b3eb14a7a936dddefb2d78e224dbeb01d2358.\n\nFollowing the [working mode's guidance on anchors](https://whatwg.org/working-mode#anchors), I would kindly request that these anchors be kept permanently available in the Living Standard. The last two are generated from heading text, so they would change if those headings were reworded.\n\nThank in advance!",
